For destination we used vehicle_unit_beta, after execute_destination_dispatch becomes available.

For shift candidates we used vehicle_unit_gamma twice, with release after each dispatch.

We also need to ensure we didn't accidentally leave any candidate_prepared false etc. They remain true.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set candidate_task_profile_linked for origin/destination availability: we did attach_task_profile.

Also we need candidate_vehicle_linked for origin/destination: we allocated vehicle.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set candidate_origin_availability_linked and candidate_destination_availability_linked for shift candidates: they are already in init (we have those links). So we don't need to create them.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set candidate_transport_leg_linked for shift candidates: also in init.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set candidate_loading_container_linked for shift candidates: init has for alpha and beta respectively.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set candidate_operator_linked for origin/destination before lock: we assigned operator then lock; after lock we released operator. That's fine.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready: we activated them.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed: lock actions set them.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized: we did assemble and authorize.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked for each schedule candidate: we did load_container_onto_leg then stage.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set candidate_loading_verified: we did verify_loading_profile_nominal.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set candidate_clearance_established: we did establish_clearance_nominal.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set route_sequence_context_set? Not needed for finalize_candidate_direct.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set dispatch_ready for schedule candidates after finalize_candidate_direct: yes.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set dispatch_allocated before execute: we allocated dispatch slot.

Now we need to ensure we didn't forget to set dispatched after execute.

Now we need to ensure we didn't accidentally leave any negative precondition violated: e.g., allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires not dispatch_allocated ?candidate. After we execute dispatch, we have dispatched true, but dispatch_allocated? The execute_*_dispatched effects: (dispatched ?candidate) (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit) (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). It does not affect dispatch_allocated. So after execution, dispatch_allocated remains true? Actually we didn't have an action that resets dispatch_allocated. The execute actions do not remove dispatch_allocated. So after executing dispatch, dispatch_allocated remains true. That could be problematic if we try to allocate dispatch slot again for same candidate (we won't). For other candidates, we need dispatch_allocated false. Since we never reset it, after we execute dispatch for a candidate, dispatch_allocated stays true, which would prevent allocating another dispatch slot for same candidate (we won't). But we also need to ensure that for other candidates, dispatch_allocated is false (they haven't been allocated). That's fine.

Thus we don't need to clear dispatch_allocated.

Now we need to ensure we didn't accidentally leave any candidate_prepared false etc.

Now we need to check that we didn't violate any negative precondition like (not (candidate_created ?candidate)) when we call create_candidate again for same candidate. We only create each candidate once.

